Ryujinx StructuredProgram: the Ampere front end's cooperative-matrix instruction (ampere-coopmat-instruction.patch) returns its
destination registers as one vector, like TextureSample. Same file as structured-program-cfg-check.patch: the csproj applies this
one to that patch's output (ShaderPatch metadata `Then`). The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
--- a/StructuredIr/StructuredProgram.cs
+++ b/StructuredIr/StructuredProgram.cs
@@ -424,7 +424,8 @@
             return inst switch
             {
                 Instruction.ImageLoad or
-                Instruction.TextureSample => true,
+                Instruction.TextureSample or
+                Instruction.CooperativeMatrixMulAdd => true,   // Ampere front end: one word per destination register
                 _ => false,
             };
         }
